  "agent": {
    "note": "**Found and fixed the missing cursor.** Good catch — it was a real bug, and the diagnosis is worth keeping.\n\n**Root cause — NOT a layer/depth issue, and NOT chunking.** On a transparent base (`color=black@0`), ffmpeg's `drawbox` **blends RGB but never writes the alpha channel**, so the orange edges came out `(255,138,61, alpha 0)` — right color, zero opacity. They survive an `rgb24` probe (alpha ignored — which is exactly why my earlier 'cursor present' check lied to me) but **vanish the instant the layer is alpha-composited onto the tiles**. So the graph was perfect, rendered fine in isolation, and composited to nothing.\n\n**Fix:** `replace=1` on every drawbox — it *replaces* the pixel (RGB **and** alpha) instead of blending, so the edges are opaque and survive the overlay. One word.\n\n**Verified:**\n\n| check | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| drawbox edge alpha | 0 (invisible) | opaque |\n| overlay onto solid bg | 0 orange px | 4992 orange px |\n| 4×4 render (no chunk) | no ring | ring at exact bounds ✓ |\n| **8×8 render (spatial-chunked)** | no ring | ring tracks the walk ✓ |\n\nThe perf win is untouched — still ONE lavfi source, one overlay layer, drawbox per step (canvas −76% on 4×4). I confirmed the ring at 8×8 specifically because that's where you hit it (64 tiles → the canvas spatial-chunks; the fix holds through that path).\n\n*(14 canvas tests green, now asserting `replace=1`. Learning written up — `.ai/candidates/2026-06-29-drawbox-track-collapse.md` — with the alpha gotcha front and center: never trust an rgb24 probe on a maskless transparent-base lavfi; check alpha.)*",
    "question": "Render this 8×8 and confirm the orange ring is back and tracking the parse correctly (it was the scale where it broke). One-liner:\n\n`node packages/cli/dist/index.js make packages/sandbox/sessions/2026-06-28-dsl-tutorial/candidate-020.mosaicx -w 1280 -h 720 -o packages/sandbox/sessions/2026-06-28-dsl-tutorial/candidate-020.mp4`\n\nIf the ring reads right, the canvas collapse is truly done and the next bottleneck is **dsl-string**. If anything's still off (thickness/color/timing at this scale), tell me.",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "other",
        "label": "canvas-perf-drawbox-fix"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "propose",
        "summary": "Fix invisible drawbox cursor (replace=1 — drawbox didn't write alpha on a transparent base, edges dropped under compositing); perf win from 019 preserved; verified at 4×4 and 8×8."
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "019"
      }
    }
  }
